/*!
\mainpage Validose Ophthalmic Firmware Documentation

\section intro_sec Introduction
This documentation provides an overview of the firmware developed for the Validose Ophthalmic
The firmware is designed to ensure compliance with the IEC 62304 standard for medical device software lifecycle processes 
and adheres to other relevant standards including ISO 14971 for risk management.

\section purpose_sec Purpose

\section compliance_sec Compliance
The firmware was developed in accordance with the following standards:
- IEC 62304: Software Lifecycle Processes for Medical Devices.
- ISO 14971: Application of Risk Management to Medical Devices.

\section features_sec Key Features
- Safety-Critical Design: Implements robust error handling and recovery mechanisms.
- Peripheral Integration: The device includes the following peripherals:
 - Accurate stimulation current and voltage sensing,
 - A 6-axis IMU for gesture and significant motion detection,
 - Accurate current controlled stimulation circuit.
- Power Efficiency: Optimized for low power consumption.
- Modular Design: Allows for easy scalability, maintenance, and testing.

\section architecture_sec Firmware Architecture
The firmware follows a layered and modular architecture to ensure maintainability, scalability, and testability. 
The architecture is structured into the following major groups.
- Modules - High-level application functionality.
- Drivers - Low-level hardware drivers for the system.
- Common - Units common to both Modules and Drivers.

For a detailed breakdown of the architecture, refer to the firmware architecture document and the [Modules](modules.html) section in this document.
Each module has a defined interface through which other modules and units interact with the module in question. These interfaces can be found in each respective module's files, where the file name follows the convention **module_name_interface.h**. 
Details of the interface functions can be examined by expanding the interface struct definition in the relevant sections of this document.  

\section usage_sec Firmware Usage

\subsection directory_structure Directory Structure
The firmware directory structure can be found in the [Files](files.html) section of this document.

\subsection building Building the Firmware
The firmware is built using the following toolchain. Versions of all the tools and dependencies can be found in the SBOM.
- NRF5 SDK
- GCC
- Make

To build the project, follow the instructions here: \ref build_page .

\section compatibility Compatibility Note

This firmware release is designed and tested for compatibility with specific hardware versions.

